    "conventional_translations": ["enthymeme", "rhetorical syllogism"],
    "aristotle_usage": "The rhetorical syllogism/deduction; the body of persuasion; drawn from probabilities and signs using fewer premises than a full syllogism. Literally 'something held in the mind.'",
